        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Confusing Display"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(concentrate, emotion, enchantment, fear, incapacitation, mental, occult, visual)\n\nThe augnagar's writhing limbs and flesh seethe and squirm in a disorienting and unsettling manner. Creatures in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a 34 Will save, after which they are temporarily immune to further Confusing Displays for 1 minute.\n\n- **Critical Success:** The creature is unaffected.\n- **Success:** The creature is stupefied 1 for 1 round.\n- **Failure:** The creature is stupefied 1 and confused for 1 minute.\n- **Critical Failure:** As failure, but the creature can't attempt a flat check to recover from confusion whenever it takes damage from an attack or spell."
            },
            "action_type": {
              "value": "none"
            },
            "action_cost": {
              "value": "two_actions"
            },
            "action_attack_bonus": {
              "value": 0
            },
            "action_damage_variants": {
              "value": []
            },
            "id": "50ba8531-c309-4e19-b46a-5bfd92f7981a",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-19T22:58:51.312291"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Inhale Vitality"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(necromancy, occult)\n\nFrequency once per day; The augnagar inhales sharply, drawing life force out of creatures in a 50-foot cone. Creatures in the area take 14d6 negative damage (34 basic Fortitude save, and the creature is fatigued on a failure). The augnagar becomes quickened for 1 round on its next turn, and it can use the extra action only to Stride or Strike."
            },
            "action_type": {
              "value": "none"
            },
